ar on the leading edge)."],[1542,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1736,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[613,"`overlay=\"popover\"` always uses the desktop presentation."],[615,"`pageCount` sets months per popover page: one for single dates and two for ranges by default."],[1104,"`PaginationDots` is decorative and does not replace interactive page\ncontrols."],[876,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[864,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[1121,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[867,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1149,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1154,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1237,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[1062,"`role=\"d